# r17 DIAGNOSTIC - T25c/O14: returning an existing read-only reference from a function whose bare "&" result is built
# says "a read-only reference cannot become writable - pass a writable one, or drop the 'mut'". No "mut" is written
# anywhere; the result is writable only because a built result is (T25b), and the fix is to borrow the result -
# "fn first(l List<Item&>&) Item&l". Seen five times in this study (removeNamed, Map values, Pratt locals, fold). In
# the Pratt case (r04) the attached note says "declare it 'lhs mut E&' to write through it", which drops the "&return"
# the local needs and leads straight to O10d.
#
# expected: an error naming the built result and suggesting Item&l
# actual: error[T25c] at line 12 as quoted
type Item struct(name String&) { name }
fn first(l List<Item&>&) Item& {
    return l[0]
}
fn main() ? {
    l := List<Item&>()
    l.Push(Item("a"))
    println(first(l).name)
}
